MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Looped our latest solvers over all ARC-AGI-3 games (bounded, conflict-safe:
read-only checkpoints, no registry races vs the conductor's active ARC work).

Forward progress found: tu93 L1 -> L2. graph_explore_solve_v2, run from the
REPLAYED L1 state (not cold), reaches L2; the full L1+L2 path (43 actions) is
reproduction-gated (reached_level=2, reproduced=True) and saved. Registry tu93
1->2; gate eval (carnot policy) 24 -> 25/183 levels.

Honest nulls (the rest are at their current solver's frontier): lp85 L4->L5 no
advance (verifier-routed search found no winning L5 path within depth caps);
the other 9 graph_explore L1 games found no L2; the unsolved L0 games (vc33,
dc22, s5i5, sb26, re86, ...) found no L1 -- those need the world-model / per-game
RE approaches the conductor is actively building (E3, learned A* heuristic), not
more graph-explore. Offline, air-gapped, zero quota, nothing submitted.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
